# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SatQuery AI — Frontend Environment Variables
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values.
# NEVER commit the .env file to version control.
# The .env file is already listed in .gitignore.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ─── Backend ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FastAPI backend base URL.
#   Development : http://localhost:8000
#   Production  : https://your-deployed-backend.example.com
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000


# ─── Google Maps Platform ───────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Required for the Google Earth-style 3D satellite map experience.
# Get your key at: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#
# APIs you must enable in Google Cloud Console for the key to work:
#   1. Maps JavaScript API     — core map, satellite imagery, 3D terrain
#   2. Street View Static API  — 360° panorama imagery
#   3. Places API              — location search autocomplete & suggestions
#   4. Geocoding API           — converts Place IDs to lat/lng coordinates
#
# How to restrict your API key (strongly recommended):
#   Cloud Console → Credentials → [your key] → Application restrictions
#   → HTTP referrers (websites) → add your domains:
#     For production : https://yourdomain.com/*
#     For development: http://localhost:5173/*
#                      http://localhost:4173/*   (vite preview)
#
# Billing note:
#   Google Maps requires a billing account. New accounts receive a
#   $200/month free credit which covers typical development usage.
#   Map loads, Street View loads, and Places calls each have separate
#   pricing — see: https://mapsplatform.google.com/pricing/
#
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=


# ─── AI Chat (Groq) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Powers the in-app AI chat panel (Llama 3.3-70b via Groq).
# Get your free key at: https://console.groq.com/keys
VITE_GROQ_API_KEY=


# ─── App ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_APP_ENV=development


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# QUICK START
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# 1. Copy this file:
#      cp .env.example .env
#
# 2. Fill in VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY with your Google Maps key.
#    Enable the four APIs listed above in Google Cloud Console.
#
# 3. (Optional) Add VITE_API_BASE_URL if you have a local backend.
#
# 4. Run the development server:
#      npm run dev
#
# 5. Open http://localhost:5173
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
